    "thm-abc-zero-tolerance-target-is-summary-posterior-under-density-regularity": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Countable Choice. In the proper prior-simulator model of [[def-approximate-bayesian-computation]], let $d\\ge1$, $s_0\\in\\mathbb R^d$, and suppose the summary-predictive measure has a specified jointly measurable density version\n$$M(d\\theta,ds)=m_\\theta(s)\\,\\Pi(d\\theta)\\,\\lambda_d(ds),$$\nwhere $\\lambda_d$ is Lebesgue measure on $\\mathbb R^d$ ([[def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra]]). Assume that $s\\mapsto m_\\theta(s)$ is continuous at $s_0$ for $\\Pi$-almost every $\\theta$, that a measurable $H:\\Theta\\to[0,\\infty]$ satisfies\n$$m_\\theta(s)\\le H(\\theta)\\quad\\text{for $\\Pi$-almost every $\\theta$ and every }\\|s-s_0\\|_2\\le\\epsilon_0$$\nfor some $\\epsilon_0>0$ and $\\int H\\,d\\Pi<\\infty$, and that\n$$0<z_0:=\\int_\\Theta m_\\theta(s_0)\\,\\Pi(d\\theta)<\\infty.$$\nDefine the density-selected summary posterior\n$$\\Pi^m_{s_0}(A):=\\frac{\\int_A m_\\theta(s_0)\\,\\Pi(d\\theta)}{z_0}.$$\nThen, for all sufficiently small $\\epsilon>0$ for which the target is defined, the indicator ABC target $\\Pi_\\epsilon(\\cdot\\mid s_0)$ converges to $\\Pi^m_{s_0}$ in total variation as $\\epsilon\\downarrow0$.\n\nThe pointwise density version is part of the statement. The conclusion is the density-selected summary update; it does not claim that every regular conditional distribution has that value at a null summary value."
    ],
    "thm-sufficient-summary-recovers-full-posterior": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume AC. Let $(\\Theta,\\mathcal T)$, $(\\mathsf Y,\\mathcal Y)$, and $(\\mathsf T,\\mathcal C)$ be standard Borel spaces ([[def-standard-borel-space]]), let $\\Pi$ be a proper prior, and let $K$ be a sampling probability kernel as in [[def-bayesian-model-as-prior-and-sampling-kernel]]. Let $S:\\mathsf Y\\to\\mathsf T$ be a measurable statistic ([[def-statistic-and-estimator]]) that is sufficient in the common-kernel sense of [[def-sufficient-statistic]]. Write $K_S(\\theta,C)=K(\\theta,S^{-1}(C))$, let $M$ be the joint prior-predictive law of $(\\theta,S(Y))$, and let $J_Y$ and $J_S$ be the data and summary marginals. A posterior kernel $\\Pi^S_t$ of $\\theta$ given $S(Y)=t$ exists. Then\n$$\\widehat\\Pi_y(A):=\\Pi^S_{S(y)}(A)$$\nis a data-indexed posterior version for the full observation: for every $A\\in\\mathcal T$ and $D\\in\\mathcal Y$,\n$$J(\\Theta\\in A,Y\\in D)=\\int_D\\widehat\\Pi_y(A)\\,J_Y(dy).$$\nThus full-data posterior information is preserved by a sufficient summary, up to the usual almost-everywhere version convention.\n\nIn a dominated branch, suppose $\\mu$ and $\\nu$ are sigma-finite reference measures for the full data and summary, respectively, and the specified jointly measurable densities satisfy\n$$K(\\theta,dy)=p_\\theta(y)\\,\\mu(dy),\\qquad K_S(\\theta,dt)=h_\\theta(t)\\,\\nu(dt),\\qquad p_\\theta(y)=g(y)h_\\theta(S(y))$$\non the specified common versions, with $g:\\mathsf Y\\to[0,\\infty]$ independent of $\\theta$. For any $y$ where the factorization holds $\\Pi$-almost everywhere, $0<g(y)<\\infty$, and\n$$0<Z_S(S(y)):=\\int_\\Theta h_\\theta(S(y))\\,\\Pi(d\\theta)<\\infty,$$\nthe explicit full-data and summary posterior updates agree at $y$ by cancellation of $g(y)$. No equality is asserted on zero or infinite evidence fibres."
    ],
    "cex-abc-zero-tolerance-limit-fails-without-integrable-envelope": [
      "## Statement\n\nThere is a proper prior-simulator model with parameter space $\\mathbb N_{\\ge1}$, summary space $\\mathbb R$, and observed summary $s_0=0$ such that every parameter-specific summary density is continuous at $0$ and its prior average there is positive and finite, but the indicator ABC targets do not converge in total variation to the posterior selected by those density values. In fact, any common integrable envelope on any neighborhood of $0$ fails to exist."
