    "ex-abc-vanishing-acceptance-rate": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\Theta=\\{0,1\\}$ have equal prior probabilities and let $Y\\mid\\theta$ be uniform on $[\\theta,\\theta+1]$. With identity summary and observed value $s_0=1/2$, the ABC acceptance probability equals $\\epsilon$ for $0<\\epsilon<1/2$, so it tends to zero, while every such ABC target is $\\delta_0$ and the density-selected zero-tolerance posterior is also $\\delta_0$."
    ],
    "ex-abc-finite-sample-sufficient-summary": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\Theta=\\{1/3,2/3\\}$ have prior mass $1/2$ at each parameter. Given $\\theta$, observe three independent Bernoulli$(\\theta)$ variables $Y=(Y_1,Y_2,Y_3)$, and summarize by $S(Y)=Y_1+Y_2+Y_3$. For observed data $y_0=(1,1,0)$ and any $0\\le\\epsilon<1$, the ABC target based on $S$ equals the full-data posterior, with masses $1/3$ at $1/3$ and $2/3$ at $2/3$. The count statistic is sufficient."
